ANGLE's Vulkan backend for an iOS app, over MoltenVK. Written for aTerm (the app
crate-ios succeeds) against upstream ANGLE 9addc2983b90152f628cfdaea194983b46b254bd;
Scripts/build-angle.sh applies it.

  - BUILD.gn, system_utils.cpp: libEGL dispatches to GLESv2.framework/GLESv2, the
    one GLESv2 the app embeds, and finds it by its framework path.
  - vulkan/BUILD.gn, libvulkan_loader.cpp: open MoltenVK.framework directly; an
    app can't use the Khronos loader, which needs an ICD manifest.
  - vk_renderer.cpp: on MoltenVK, don't let the missing VK_EXT_provoking_vertex
    cap the context at ES 2.0 (Metal fixes the provoking vertex), and keep
    primitive topology static, without which MoltenVK draws a triangle fan as
    one triangle.

diff --git a/BUILD.gn b/BUILD.gn
index f38d9e8..5ab9e40 100644
--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -1465,6 +1465,12 @@ config("shared_library_public_config") {
 }
 
 _angle_glesv2_library_name = "libGLESv2${angle_libs_suffix}"
+if (is_ios) {
+  # aTerm: the app embeds ANGLE as EGL.framework and GLESv2.framework, the names
+  # libepoxy opens. libEGL must dispatch to that same GLESv2 binary; a second
+  # copy under another name would be a second ANGLE with no current context.
+  _angle_glesv2_library_name = "GLESv2"
+}
 _angle_glesv2_vulkan_secondaries_library_name =
     "libGLESv2_vulkan_secondaries${angle_libs_suffix}"
 
